{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3121","id":3341620599,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887HLRV3","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3121","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3121.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3121.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3121","number":3121,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"policy: add App Connector support via nodeAttrs","user":{"login":"matanbaruch","id":36934912,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2OTM0OTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36934912?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch","html_url":"https://github.com/matanbaruch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matanbaruch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"App connector configuration is now delivered through the `nodeAttrs` `app` field, the way Tailscale delivers it, instead of the custom `appConnectors` policy block this PR originally added. Rebased on current main.\n\nFollowing up on @Matchlighter's suggestion: after #3251 landed nodeAttrs, the only missing piece was valued capabilities. `nodeAttrs` carried key-only caps through `attr` and nothing else.\n\n## What changed\n\n1. `NodeAttrGrant` gets an `app` field (`tailcfg.NodeCapMap`), stamped into the node's CapMap in `compileNodeAttrs` next to the key-only attrs. Payloads are passed through opaquely and the client interprets them.\n2. App connectors ride that generic path, so there is no app-connector-specific code left anywhere: `compileNodeAttrs` -> `NodeCapMap` -> `NodesWithChangedCapMap` -> `SelfUpdate`.\n3. The `PolicyChange{IncludeSelf: true}` broadcast the first version needed is gone. A reload now sends a targeted self update only to nodes whose config actually changed, which also fixes the reload propagation @dmeremyanin hit.\n4. Removed: the `appConnectors` block, the `AppConnector` / `AppConnectorAttr` types, `AppConnectorConfigForNode` and its wrappers, the `builder.go` injection, and the load-time domain validation.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tagOwners\": {\n    \"tag:connector\": [\"admin@\"]\n  },\n  \"nodeAttrs\": [\n    {\n      \"target\": [\"tag:connector\"],\n      \"app\": {\n        \"tailscale.com/app-connectors\": [\n          {\n            \"name\": \"Internal Apps\",\n            \"connectors\": [\"tag:connector\"],\n            \"domains\": [\"internal.example.com\", \"*.corp.example.com\"],\n            \"routes\": [\"10.0.0.0/8\"]\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n## What works and what does not\n\nWorks today: the capability reaches every node the `target` selects, hardcoded `routes` are advertised as soon as the connector gets its config, and policy reloads propagate.\n\nDoes not work yet: Headscale does not tell clients to send DNS queries for the configured domains to the connector, so dynamic domain discovery does not happen on its own. That is the DNS side of the feature and it belongs with the v0.31 work. `docs/ref/policy.md` says so in a warning admonition, `features.md` marks App Connectors unchecked with the delivery part checked underneath, so nobody reads this as done.\n\nTwo deliberate behavior notes:\n\n1. The cap ships on `target` match regardless of `tailscale set --advertise-connector`. This matches Tailscale, where the client gates on its local connector flag and on the payload's `connectors` field.\n2. No load-time domain validation. Payloads are pass through, so a malformed domain surfaces client side.\n\n## Cap name validation\n\nGrant `app` cap names go through `validateCapabilityName`, which rejects URL-formatted names and `tailscale.com/*` names that are not in `tailscaleCapAllowlist`. The `app` field on nodeAttrs needs the same guard, otherwise a policy can ship any `tailscale.com` capability to a node with nothing behind it:\n\n```json\n{ \"target\": [\"*\"], \"app\": { \"tailscale.com/cap/funnel\": [] } }\n```\n\nSo there is a `validateNodeCapabilityName` with its own allowlist, currently holding only `tailscale.com/app-connectors`. It is a separate map because `tailscaleCapAllowlist` is keyed by `tailcfg.PeerCapability` and its comment is about peer caps. Names in an operator's own domain, like `example.com/app/my-cap`, still pass through. The reasoning is the one already in `nodeAttrUnsupportedCaps`: rejecting at load beats letting a node advertise something that does not work.\n\nIf you would rather have one shared allowlist, or no gate at all on the nodeAttrs side, say so and I will change it.\n\n## Tests\n\nUnit (`hscontrol/policy/v2/appconnector_test.go`), on the shared nodeAttrs fixtures:\n\n1. `TestAppConnectorViaNodeAttrs`: targeted node gets both configs, non-targeted nodes get nothing, `routes` round trips through `appctype.AppConnectorAttr`.\n2. `TestAppConnectorWildcardTarget`: `*` reaches every node.\n3. `TestAppConnectorChangeTracking`: the cap participates in `NodesWithChangedCapMap`, which is what makes the `IncludeSelf` removal safe.\n4. `TestValidateNodeCapabilityName` and `TestAppConnectorUnsupportedCapRejected`: the allowlist, both at the helper and at policy load.\n\nIntegration (`integration/appconnector_test.go`): `TestAppConnectorBasic`, `TestAppConnectorNonMatchingTag`, `TestAppConnectorWildcardConnector`. Configs are marshalled through `appctype.AppConnectorAttr` so the tests use the same wire shape a Tailscale hosted control plane emits.\n\nUpdates #1651\n\n- [x] have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md) file\n- [x] raised a GitHub issue or discussed it on the projects chat beforehand\n- [x] added unit tests\n- [x] added integration tests\n- [x] updated documentation if needed\n- [x] updated CHANGELOG.md\n","created_at":"2026-03-01T20:10:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-08T22:47:24Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_ur